From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: use the versions repo for update feeds and compare by version instead
 of commit

VSCodium serves update metadata from its own versions repository as latest.json feeds keyed by quality/platform/architecture/target, so the feed URL is rebuilt from productService.updateUrl and availability is decided by comparing normalized semantic versions rather than the upstream commit id, which VSCodium builds do not share (#2211, #2216, #2777). The rework also threads through Windows MSI installer updates via msiexec (#2843, #2853).

